{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For the people fled.</b> That they did not travel through the wilderness in a straight line, as they had announced in saying דֶּרֶךְ שְׁלֹשֶׁת יָמִים נֵלֵךְ בַּמִּדְבָּר (Exodus 8:23), but turned back on their tracks as fugitives not knowing the way." "<b>And the heart of Pharaoh turned.</b> For he thought that Baal Zephon had power against the blessed El." "<b>What is this we have done, that we sent them away.</b> And we did not inquire of Baal Zephon, who was our helper — and we would not have been compelled to send them away."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:24.620148091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}